# Second Opinion — AI Scam Checker

An AI-powered tool that helps people identify suspicious messages, understand potential scam indicators, and make safer decisions before clicking links or sending money.

**Project status:** Hackathon prototype in development. Features, test results, and deployment details will be updated as they are implemented and verified.

---

## 1. Overview

Second Opinion is an AI-assisted scam detection application designed to help people evaluate suspicious messages before acting on them.

Users can submit a suspicious text message and, where supported by the implementation, a URL for analysis. The application examines potential warning signs, combines model-generated analysis with deterministic checks, and returns a clear explanation of the findings.

Rather than simply labelling a message as a scam, Second Opinion aims to explain why a message may be suspicious and what the user should do next.

The project uses an NVIDIA Nemotron open model through Nebius Token Factory to analyse message content and generate plain-English explanations.

### The problem

Online scams often exploit urgency, impersonation, misleading links, and requests for money or personal information. Many people struggle to distinguish legitimate communications from fraudulent ones, especially when messages imitate trusted organisations.

Second Opinion aims to make scam awareness more accessible by providing an additional layer of analysis before a user takes action.

### Our approach

*   Analyse suspicious message text.
*   Identify potential scam indicators and suspicious URL patterns.
*   Explain findings in plain English.
*   Communicate uncertainty rather than promising perfect detection.
*   Recommend cautious next steps that users can take independently.

