### Target audience

*   People who receive suspicious text messages or emails.
*   Students and young adults who shop, communicate, and transact online.
*   Older adults and people who want additional help evaluating unfamiliar messages.
*   Families supporting relatives who may be vulnerable to scams.
*   Anyone who wants a second opinion before interacting with a suspicious message.

### Project goals

1.  Make scam analysis understandable to non-technical users.
2.  Explain the evidence behind each assessment.
3.  Combine AI interpretation with transparent, rule-based checks.
4.  Handle uncertain cases responsibly.
5.  Demonstrate how open AI models can support practical fraud-awareness tools.

